  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN238.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">iravukkuṟi vanta talaimakaṟkut tōḻi collitu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the confidante said to HIM who came to the night tryst.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN238.1">
        <l>māṉṟamai yaṟiyā marampa<supplied>yi</supplied> liṟumpi</l>
        <l>ṉīṉṟiḷaip paṭṭa vayavuppiṇai pacitteṉa</l>
        <l>maṭamāṉ valci tarīiya naṭunā</l>
        <l>ḷirumukaic cilampi ṉiraivēṭ ṭeḻunta</l>
        <l>paṇaimaru<anchor n="1"/> ḷe<supplied>ru</supplied>ttiṟ palvari yirumpōttu</l>
        <l>maṭakka ṇāmāṉ mātirat <supplied>talaṟat</supplied></l>
        <l>taṭakkōṭ ṭāmā ṉaṇṇa lēṟu</l>
        <l>naṉantalaik kāṉattu <supplied>va</supplied>lampaṭat tolaicci</l>
        <l>yiruṅkal viyaliṟai vicippa vīrkkum</l>
        <l>peruṅka ṉāṭa piriti yāyiṉ</l>
        <l>maruntu muṭaiyaiyō maṟṟē yirappōrk</l>
        <l>kiḻaiyaṇi neṭuntēr kaḷiṟō ṭeṉṟu</l>
        <l>maḻaicuran taṉṉa vīkai vaṇmakiḻ</l>
        <l>kaḻaṟoṭit taṭakkaik kalimā ṉaḷḷi</l>
        <l>naḷimukai yuṭaitta naṟuṅkā raṭukkattup</l>
        <l>pōntai muḻumuta<anchor n="2"/> ṉilaiiya <supplied>kān</supplied>taṇ</l>
        <l>meṉpiṇi mukaiyaviḻn talarāt</l>
        <l>taṇkamaḻ putumalar nāṟunaṟu nutaṟkē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="10a-c">O man from the land of big stones,</l>
        <l corresp="3">where, at midday, when the youthful stag gives food,</l>
        <l corresp="2">because [its] doe, that was exhausted after giving birth, is hungry with cravings,</l>
        <l corresp="1">in the rustling thicket of trees that is not knowm to have been disturbed,</l>
        <l corresp="5">the large male with many stripes, with a bamboo-like neck,</l>
        <l corresp="4">that has risen to hunt for food on the mountain-side with dark caves,</l>
        <l corresp="8">destroyed, for it to fall on [its] ride side, in the forest of vast space,</l>
        <l corresp="7">the majestic wild bull with broad horns,</l>
        <l corresp="6">so that the wild cow with innocent eyes cries out in [all] directions,</l>
        <l corresp="9">[and] drags [it] along, in order to secure it on the wide eave of dark stones,</l>
        <l rend="indent6" corresp="10d">if you were to part,</l>
        <l corresp="11a-c">would you possess the remedy too?</l>
        <l corresp="18">– for [her with] fragrant forehead, fragrant of cool-smelling fresh flowers,</l>
        <l corresp="17">blooming after the buds opened [their] soft fetters,</l>
        <l corresp="16">of the Malabar lily that stayed on the whole trunk of the palmyra tree</l>
        <l corresp="15">on the mountain side, in the fragrant rainy season that has broken the tight buds,</l>
        <l corresp="14">[belonging to] Naḷḷi with spirited horses [and] broad hands with loose armlets</l>
        <l corresp="12d-13">that rejoice in always giving liberally, like rain streaming down,</l>
        <l corresp="12a-c">jewel-adorned tall chariots along with elephant bulls</l>
        <l rend="indent6" corresp="11d">to those who request [him].</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>


